//? Title: Sundaram sieve: actual odd-composite factor strikes
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Sundaram marks odd-composite indices and emits the unmarked odd primes, with2
handled separately. Actual pair strikes and marker transitions replace the old
report-side re-sieve.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For k=floor((limit-1)/2), index m=i+j+2ij maps to2m+1=(2i+1)(2j+1). Thus
striking all1<=i<=j with m<=k removes every odd composite and no odd prime. Each
unmarked i>=1 emits2i+1; emit2 separately when allowed by the inclusive bound.
Marker repeats are real work, counted separately from first marks.
Division-based bounds and stepped indices avoid overflow in the pair expression.
O(limit log limit) is an upper bound, with odd-index linear storage; no
wall-time comparison is claimed.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/sundaram_sieve_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::sundaram_trace(30);
    std::print("| actual i | j | odd index | mapped composite | first mark |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "--- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.i, s.j, s.index,
                   2 * s.index + 1, s.newly_marked);
    std::print("Actual primes `{}`.\n", r.primes);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Inclusive bound30; odd indices1..14");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual pair strikes", r.strikes));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual primes", r.primes.size()));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/sundaram_sieve_tiny.svg");
}
```
