> API and interpretation

Complete odd-marker geometry is checked before allocation and actual
strikes/capture have separate policies. Default limits bound practical
memory/work; a uint64 bound does not imply every such bound can be materialized.
The report uses actual producer marker flags and does not independently
reimplement the sieve for its figure.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- Sundaram, odd-composite sieve (1934); factor identity derived explicitly above

